{"kind":"assert","text":"Source answer to e227be18 at main 4cef11d2783efaa591fac197d9a2ba093004456e: retirement has two different paths. A retired Grow object does no archive pass. A current object whose admitted archive target reaches the retired directory keeps returning retry/unavailable; the driver does not turn directory retirement into a terminal named stop or throw it out of the archive pass.\n\nThe object first classifies its storage. A populated store without the current format marker counts as retired (packages/scope/src/room-format.ts:11–31). Its constructor returns before scope wiring (packages/scope/src/object.ts:194–202), and alarm() returns immediately at line 963. That alarm returns void, not an ArchivePass stopped result, and does not schedule another archive wake.\n\nFor a current, archive-admitted object, the stale directory setting remains syntactically valid: growArchiveConfiguration checks its shape and trusted release, not directory liveness (apps/room/archive.ts:26–34). A retired nativeBirth RPC returns {stop:\"retired\"} (packages/scope/src/object.ts:808–819); namespace birth reads turn that into null (packages/scope/src/namespace.ts:443–452). If discovery instead reaches archiveItem, that RPC also returns the retired stop (packages/scope/src/object.ts:782–784), and the Grow resolver converts it to unavailable (apps/room/archive.ts:61–66). Failed birth/query discovery yields no target; the Grow resolver returns null rather than an alternate repository (packages/scope/src/archive-target.ts:64–89,124–145; apps/room/archive.ts:78–83).\n\nBefore target I/O, the production driver records its next retry: pending work increments its attempt with capped exponential backoff; a pass before a pending Mark defers by the initial retry interval. A missing target then returns {state:\"retry\",next:scheduled,reason:\"unavailable\"}; it neither disables the driver nor records a stop (packages/scope/src/archive-driver.ts:134–141,193–212). run() retains that next wake (lines 128–132). alarm() awaits the pass and always arbitrates wakes afterward (packages/scope/src/object.ts:980–991); Wakes.set includes the archive wake (packages/scope/src/outbox.ts:80–89). With a valid clock and functioning storage, each due pass retries while that target remains unavailable. Target exceptions inside the pass likewise become retry/unavailable (packages/scope/src/archive-driver.ts:451–459).\n\nThe premise matters: a pre-existing stopped row returns its stored named stop before discovery; an unadmitted definition or unsupported policy disables archive instead (packages/scope/src/archive-driver.ts:178–186). Missing/invalid archive configuration or binding creates no Grow archive driver (apps/room/archive.ts:40–42). A current room under another directory also fails the configured-directory check and follows the same target-missing retry path (apps/room/archive.ts:63,78–80). The stale setting alone therefore does not imply that every Grow object retries. This retirement path does not throw; unrelated alarm owners or wake-storage failures remain outside that conclusion.\n\nI read source only. I ran no tests, builds, compilers, servers, provider commands or deployment commands and changed no source.","body":{"to":"planner"}}